WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:08.387
Installing PageMotor on HostGator. It is standard cPanel, about ten minutes, and you do not need to be technical.

2
00:00:08.387 --> 00:00:11.303
One thing to check before you start, though.

3
00:00:12.003 --> 00:00:18.428
The plan. HostGator's standard hosting plans all include cPanel, which is what PageMotor needs.

4
00:00:18.428 --> 00:00:24.312
Their separate Website Builder product does not, and PageMotor cannot run there at all.

5
00:00:24.312 --> 00:00:28.303
If your dashboard has no cPanel button, that is the reason.

6
00:00:29.003 --> 00:00:37.426
To open cPanel, log in at portal.hostgator.com, choose Hosting in the menu, and click the cPanel button under Quick Links.

7
00:00:37.426 --> 00:00:47.161
There is also a shortcut that always works: go to yourdomain.com/cpanel and log in with the cPanel details from your HostGator welcome email.

8
00:00:47.861 --> 00:00:54.835
In cPanel, open File Manager and go to the folder for your site, usually public_html.

9
00:00:54.835 --> 00:01:06.240
Click Upload, choose the PageMotor zip, and let it finish. File Manager takes files up to 500 MB, far larger than anything PageMotor ships.

10
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:16.004
Then right-click the zip and choose Extract. You should end up with pagemotor.php, a lib folder, and config-sample.php.

11
00:01:16.704 --> 00:01:22.056
The database is three quick stages on one page. Open MySQL Databases.

12
00:01:22.056 --> 00:01:27.331
Under Create New Database, type a name like pagemotor and create it.

13
00:01:27.331 --> 00:01:35.011
Scroll down to MySQL Users, add a new user, let the generator make the password, and write it down.

14
00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:44.475
Then scroll to Add User To Database, choose your user and your database, click Add, tick ALL PRIVILEGES, and Make Changes.

15
00:01:45.175 --> 00:01:51.865
And here is the one thing nearly everyone misses. cPanel puts your account name on the front of both.

16
00:01:51.865 --> 00:01:59.086
A database you typed as pagemotor is saved as something like theaccount_pagemotor, and the user the same way.

17
00:01:59.086 --> 00:02:07.698
Copy the full names exactly as cPanel shows them. Getting this wrong is the most common reason the install fails at the last step.

18
00:02:08.398 --> 00:02:16.585
Then rename config-sample.php to exactly config.php. That rename is what switches PageMotor on.

19
00:02:16.585 --> 00:02:26.324
Put the three values in, using the full prefixed names, and leave everything else alone. DB_HOST stays localhost.

20
00:02:27.024 --> 00:02:35.836
Then go straight to /admin/. On that first visit PageMotor sets itself up and walks you into creating your admin user.

21
00:02:35.836 --> 00:02:39.795
Open the admin before you open the front of the site.

22
00:02:40.495 --> 00:02:48.921
If you hit a 500 or a blank page, it is almost always config.php: wrong name, wrong folder, or never renamed.

23
00:02:48.921 --> 00:02:58.197
HostGator gives you three ways to read the real reason. cPanel, Metrics, Errors. The error_log file in your site folder.

24
00:02:58.197 --> 00:03:05.619
Or, without opening cPanel at all, the Customer Portal under Websites, Settings, Advanced, Logs.

25
00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:14.577
And one HostGator note worth acting on once you are in. Older accounts can still default to PHP 7.4.

26
00:03:14.577 --> 00:03:24.570
PageMotor wants a modern PHP 8. Check cPanel, Software, MultiPHP Manager, and pick a PHP 8 version if you are not on one.

